Storage is tied up to the POD lifecycle.
pod dies then storage deleted


Persistent storage in Kubernetes

Persistent volume (pv) -> Persistem volume claim(PVC) -> Storage class(SC)
storage disk like aws ebs volume -> request for storage -> storage type

Pod -> PVC -> PV (manually)
Pod -> PVC -> Storage type -> PV ( automatic)


CSI (container storage interface) Driver:
Kubernetes doesn't talk to directly to cloud storage 
It uses CSI drivers

Pod -> PVC -> Storageclass -> AWS EBS CSI driver -> create and mount EBS volume 

$ kubectl get storageclass 
( by default when use eks gp2 is available)
$ vi pvc.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: demo-pvc
spec:
  accessModes:
  - ReadWriteOnce
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 5Gi
  storageClassName: gp2

